<code>assert !Objects.isNull(c) => this.size() == c.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); Objects.equals(this.get(i), c.toArray()[i]);</code>

This assert statement checks that if the collection `c` is not null, then the size of the newly created `ArrayList` is equal to the size of `c`, and every element at index `i` in the new `ArrayList` is equal to the element at index `i` in the array representation of `c`.
--------------------
<code>assert !\old(c == null) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \old(c.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(c.toArray()[i]));</code>
